# BEAN Folio — runtime data
# POLICY (2026-11-11, supersedes the historical note below): runtime data is
# NO LONGER tracked. GitHub receives SOURCE-ONLY snapshots via the
# `github-clean` lineage; database + media durability comes from VERIFIED
# BACKUPS (/home/z/beanfolio-backups/, refreshed per DEVELOPMENT_SAFETY.md
# §1.7) — never from Git. Historical note: between 2026-10-27 and 2026-11-11
# db/uploads WERE tracked because sandbox restores once wiped untracked
# runtime data; those blobs remain in LOCAL history only. Local `main` must
# NEVER be pushed to any remote (see DEVELOPMENT_SAFETY.md §8).
/db/*.db
/db/*.db-journal
/db/backups/
# Isolated QA benchmark databases (GZ-BENCH-1 pins DATABASE_URL here) —
# runtime data, same protection class as /db/*.db.
/prisma/db/
/uploads/
/backups/
/data/laxii-tmp/
/public/downloads/
# Agent tool artifacts
/tool-results/

# vercel
.vercel


# typescript
*.tsbuildinfo
next-env.d.ts
local-*
.claude
.z-ai-config
*.log
dev.log
dev.out.log
test
prompt

server.log
# Skills directory
/skills/
# BEAN Folio — PG migration artifacts (contain user data incl. password hashes)
/pg-migration/

# local database (contains user data — never commit)
/db/*.db
/db/*.db-journal

# CODE GIFTZ engineering workspaces (runtime user data, like db/)
data/giftz-workspaces/

# Workspace-recovery archive volumes (large binaries; RETAINED ON DISK,
# never committed — see DEVELOPMENT_SAFETY.md)
/upload/

# NOTE: the GitHub credential vault (/.github-auth/) is intentionally NOT
# listed here — the platform snapshot drops gitignored paths, which would
# destroy the persistent auth on every recycle. It is hidden from git via
# .git/info/exclude (survives recycles, verified) and double-guarded by the
# publisher's staged-diff leak scan. NEVER commit it, never re-add it here.
